{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795220,"nonce":"JMCenGRW7s8rSvaq+r8mQy1qMx4=","title":"Integrate Yrs collaboration with RayDE document data and per-user undo","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P1\n\nScope\nPrototype and pin Yrs/native and compatible backend serialization versions. Map editor transactions and Unicode/index conventions into CRDT updates and back; track origins for per-author undo and suppress echo. Keep source data independent of editor mounting and load documents on demand. Define CRDT/document handles, ownership and bounded native IPC, plus interoperating native/backend fixtures before selecting the final library boundary.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nTwo and several concurrent clients converge under reordering, duplicate delivery and reconnect. Unicode/emoji/IME, multi-cursor operations, formatting, refactors and undo preserve intended edits. Switching/closing editor presentations releases UI resources without losing shared document state. Native/backend compatibility tests run across supported protocol/library versions.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}